# A screw thread with a run-out and a phase (an extension): an M20 made
# through its screen, turned 120° about its axis and fading out 4 mm
# before its end; then its phase edited from its helix group's
# [edit thread], and undo taking the edit back.
answer ok
key c
move 300 300
down L 300 300
up L 300 300
move 350 300
down L 350 300
up L 350 300
key esc
key x shift
move 350 300
down L 350 300
up L 350 300
menu Features|Screw Thread...
# The phase, then the run-out.
twmove 426 150
twdown L 426 150
twup L 426 150
edit 120
twmove 487 170
twdown L 487 170
twup L 487 170
edit 4
tw
dump
# Flip the direction: against the circle's normal, down into the part,
# then made.
twmove 60 230
twdown L 60 230
twup L 60 230
twmove 37 260
twdown L 37 260
twup L 37 260
tw
dump
# The helix group's [edit thread]: another phase, then make it.
twmove 200 110
twdown L 200 110
twup L 200 110
twmove 426 150
twdown L 426 150
twup L 426 150
edit 300
twmove 37 260
twdown L 37 260
twup L 37 260
tw
dump
# Undo takes the edit back at once.
key z ctrl
tw
dump
